  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DIB supporting KOKO Networks clean ethanol cooking for peri-urban and near-rural households in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KOKO focusses on mainstreaming liquid bio-ethanol cooking fuel as a fast, safe and affordable alternative to dirty cooking fuels such as charcoal.They partner with the downstream fuels industry and offer a suite of distribution, dispensing and end-use technologies.Under the SDG7 Results facillity, KOKO aims to target a new customer segment in their Greater Nairobi network.Currently, KOKO&apos;s core customers earn US$200 to US$500 per month.Through targeted marketing approaches and customer credit schemes, KOKO wants to reach households which earn around US$100 per month.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The company plans to reach 300.000 households by 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
